# The mission's own words (docs/systems/jobs.md): the commission the player
# holds from the start, the city's goals, and what the guards shout.
# Every text in <<...>> is still to write; replace it, keep the rest.

== letter commission
intent: The commission, from whoever sends the thief: the job (the Moon-Glass, through the keep's three seals), the pay, and where to begin (the harbour). Read in the rowboat at the start.
text:
<<the commission>>

== goal loot
kind: side
done: loot>=1000
intent: The city's loot goal, a side goal on the letter for the whole mission. The value (1000) is yours to tune.
text: <<the loot goal>>

== shout theft
intent: What a guard shouts when he finds a chest robbed of something precious (the seal), loud enough for the harbour to hear.
text: <<the theft shout>>
